#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087457 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "b322617c-ab21-5ce8-997f-2f10813b4280" :question/math-academy-id "e-5098" :question/problem "Plot the graph of the parametrically defined curve\n$x=t(t-6), \\,\\,\\, y=t^3, \\quad -2\\leq t \\leq 2$." :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t(t-6)$. This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t^3$. This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ | $-8$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $8$ |\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/e492a940fa95b406b60c6b0a5c438d98.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f29a511c-7868-5cb1-81f4-9d3980ad8f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084820} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b68a80-cbc5-5be5-96a2-36e49ca90c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084821} {:answer/id #uuid "2379493d-13ba-52ba-ad91-b4225afbf29b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-1